 the below the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $31K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $10K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Legence Corp. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $5.0B market cap on $2.6B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 21% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $219M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 78% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7759695847610527},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":